  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's no secret that underage children have gotten their grubby mitts on a Quest, one way or another and have began exploring the world alongside us adults. The massive issue is that they are extremely inappropriate, and sexual. And more importantly, prone to adopting the behavior the adults do. It has become both a safety concern for children, and the adults. The children are being exposed to inappropriate worlds and avatars with barely a barrier, and adults are being harassed verbally and sexually making public servers almost unbearable to be in.\n\nMy sort-of fix to this is a custom age requirement that world developers can use to restrict young children or minors of any age from joining their world. This is to protect them from the adult themes that may be riddled around the place. A second suggestion is adding an age-safety feature. Similar to hour you can block/mute certain trust ranks, like disabling avatars for Visitors, and muting Members. You can also block and mute a specific age demographic to avoid the inappropriate behaviors they flaunt about.\n\nI need to clarify children are impressionable, and adult worlds, and mature avatars are but a click away from them. And it is not hard to see where where I am coming from, if you visit any populated world. I want VrChat to be safe for all ages, therefore making it more enjoyable. I hope you consider this deepyly.",
